class.description:
[XRSettingsServer] is the settings domain [code]"xr"[/code]: it stores the OpenXR options a player or tester changes on a headset (foveation, render scale, refresh rate, variable rate shading, CPU and GPU performance levels, hand motion ranges, hand tracking) and pushes them to the [OpenXRInterface] of [XRServer]. The settings resource is an [XRSettings]; the file is [code]user://settings/xr.ini[/code] by default, in the format of [member ProjectSettings.settings/storage/format].
[b]Without a headset:[/b] values are stored, loaded and saved as usual. Values the interface can't take yet are listed by [method get_deferred_setting_names] and pushed when [XRServer] adds the OpenXR interface and again each time its session begins (foveation and the refresh rate need a running session). [member XRSettings.render_target_size_multiplier] goes to the interface as soon as it exists, before it is initialized, so it is used for the first session.
[b]Runtime support:[/b] values the runtime does not support (for example foveation on SteamVR) are stored but not pushed; [method get_unsupported_setting_names] lists them once the interface is initialized. Changing such a value prints a warning once.
[b]Changes during a session:[/b] foveation level and dynamic foveation, render scale, refresh rate, variable rate shading, performance levels and motion ranges take effect at once. [member XRSettings.foveation_with_subsampled_images] takes effect with the next session. [member XRSettings.hand_tracking_enabled] is a game-side value: the hand tracking extension itself is switched by the project setting [code]xr/openxr/extensions/hand_tracking[/code] at startup.
The defaults are the project settings [code]xr/openxr/foveation_level[/code], [code]xr/openxr/foveation_dynamic[/code] and [code]xr/openxr/foveation_with_subsampled_images[/code] and the runtime defaults for the other values. The domain is applied in [constant SettingsServer.APPLY_PHASE_SCENE]. Values out of range are clamped with a warning.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
func _ready():
	var xr_settings = Engine.get_singleton("XRSettingsServer")
	$Menu/RenderScale.value = xr_settings.get_render_target_size_multiplier()
	# Hide what the runtime can't do.
	for setting_name in xr_settings.get_unsupported_setting_names():
		$Menu.get_node(setting_name.to_pascal_case()).hide()

func _on_foveation_item_selected(index):
	Engine.get_singleton("XRSettingsServer").set_foveation_level(index)
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
public override void _Ready()
{
    GetNode<HSlider>("Menu/RenderScale").Value = XRSettingsServer.GetRenderTargetSizeMultiplier();
    // Hide what the runtime can't do.
    foreach (string settingName in XRSettingsServer.GetUnsupportedSettingNames())
    {
        GetNode<Control>("Menu").GetNode<Control>(settingName.ToPascalCase()).Hide();
    }
}

private void OnFoveationItemSelected(long index)
{
    XRSettingsServer.SetFoveationLevel((XRSettings.FoveationLevel)index);
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
[b]Note:[/b] This class only exists when the engine is built with the [code]openxr[/code] module (Windows, Linux, macOS, Android). It is missing in the Web export (WebXR is a different interface), on iOS and with [code]disable_xr=yes[/code]: check [code]Engine.has_singleton("XRSettingsServer")[/code].
